## Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to design a runtime-extensible system with clear separation between core orchestration and plug-in profilers. Emphasizes non-blocking concurrent data collection, per-profile isolation, and robust teardown.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy/Plugin pattern for runtime extensibility
- Registry for dynamic profiler discovery
- Isolation via separate workers or threads
- Unified, deterministic report aggregation

## Code Example

```typescript
interface IProfiler {
  start(): Promise<void>;
  stop(): Promise<void>;
  snapshot(): any;
}
interface IProfilerFactory {
  create(): IProfiler;
}
class ProfilerRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, IProfilerFactory>();
  register(name: string, factory: IProfilerFactory): void {
    this.map.set(name, factory);
  }
  create(name: string): IProfiler | null {
    const f = this.map.get(name);
    return f ? f.create() : null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
// Usage sketch
class CpuProfilerFactory implements IProfilerFactory {
  create(): IProfiler { return new CpuProfiler(); }
}
const registry = new ProfilerRegistry();
registry.register("cpu", new CpuProfilerFactory());
// Dynamic runtime registration possible
```

